  "_skill_md": "---\nname: trustmrr\ndescription: Internal API for trustmrr\nmetadata:\n  author: unbrowse\n  version: \"1.0\"\n  baseUrl: \"https://trustmrr.com\"\n  authMethod: \"API Key (x-goog-api-key)\"\n  endpointCount: 23\n  apiType: \"internal\"\n  category: \"web-app\"\n---\n\n# Trustmrr API\n\n> Reverse-engineered internal API. Unofficial — may change without notice.\n\n## Documentation Index\n- `SKILL.md` (this file)\n- `references/REFERENCE.md` (detailed endpoint docs)\n- `references/ENDPOINTS.json` (machine-readable endpoint catalog)\n- `scripts/api.ts` (typed client interface)\n\n## Authentication\nAPI Key (x-goog-api-key) — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.\n\n### Providing credentials\n- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).\n- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.\n- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).\n\n## Endpoints\n\n### Auth Flow (2)\n- `GET /api/auth/session` — Check the current user's authentication session.\n- `POST /$rpc/{$rpcToken}/GenerateIT` — Generate an IT (Interaction Token) for authentication.\n\n### Data Read (12)\n- `GET /{id}` — Get details for an item by its ID.\n- `GET /{id}/{id}` — Get details for an item using two IDs.\n- `GET /api/{apiId}` — Get details for a specific API by its ID.\n- `GET /api/analytics/{analyticId}` — Get details for a specific analytics report by its ID.\n- `GET /api/analytics/data/{dataId}` — Get specific analytics data by its ID.\n- `GET /api/game/random-startups` — Get a list of random startups for a game.\n- `GET /api/startup/revenue/{revenueId}` — Get revenue data for a specific startup by its ID.\n- `GET /api/tweet/{tweetId}` — Get details for a specific tweet by its ID.\n- `GET /country/{countryId}` — Get details for a specific country by its ID.\n- `GET /founder/{founderId}` — Get details for a specific founder by their ID.\n- `GET /startup/{startupId}` — Get details for a specific startup by its ID.\n- `GET /x/{xId}` — Get details for a specific item by its ID (xId).\n\n### Data Write (2)\n- `POST /api/startup/pageview/{pageviewId}` — Record a page view event for a specific page.\n- `POST /api/stats/atr` — Report Agent Time Resolution (ATR) statistics.\n\n### Search (1)\n- `POST /api/search` — Search for startups, founders, or other data.\n\n### Media (4)\n- `GET /_next/image` — Retrieve an image from the trustmrr media server.\n- `GET /styles/v1/mapbox/outdoors-v12` — Retrieve map style data from Mapbox.\n- `GET /styles/v1/mapbox/outdoors-v12/{outdoors-v12Id}` — Retrieve specific map style data from Mapbox.\n- `POST /youtubei/v1/embedded_player` — Request data from the YouTube embedded player.\n\n### Realtime (2)\n- `GET /api/analytics/realtime/map` — Get realtime map analytics data.\n- `POST /events/v2` — Send event data to the trustmrr event tracking system.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### OpenClaw (Unbrowse) workflow\n- Authenticate in the browser first (no credentials are shipped with this skill).\n- Capture fresh auth locally: run `unbrowse_capture` on an authenticated page for this domain.\n- Execute via backend gate + client browser executor: `unbrowse_replay` with `executionMode=\"backend\"`.\n\nExample:\n```text\nunbrowse_replay { service: \"trustmrr\", executionMode: \"backend\", endpoint: \"GET /{id}\" }\n```\n\nHere are a few examples to get you started using the `trustmrr` API:\n\n```typescript\n// Example: Retrieving startup details by ID.\n// Assumes you have a startup ID.\nasync function getStartupDetails(startupId: string) {\n  try {\n    const startup = await client.getStartup({ startupId });\n    console.log(\"Startup Details:\", startup);\n    return startup;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Error fetching startup details:\", error);\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Example: Recording a page view event.\n// Assumes you have a pageview ID.\nasync function recordPageView(pageviewId: string) {\n  try {\n    await client.postApiStartupPageview({ pageviewId });\n    console.log(\"Page view recorded successfully.\");\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Error recording page view:\", error);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Example: Searching for startups.\nasync function searchStartups(query: string) {\n  try {\n    const searchResults = await client.postApiSearch({ body: { query } });\n    console.log(\"Search Results:\", searchResults);\n    return searchResults;\n  } catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Error during search:\", error);\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n**Type:** Reverse-engineered internal API (unofficial)\n**Auth:** API Key (x-goog-api-key)\n**Base URL:** `https://trustmrr.com`\n**Captured Auth:** 3 auth headers, 7 session cookies\n\n## About This Skill\n\nThis skill provides access to Trustmrr's internal API — the hidden endpoints that power their web/mobile app.\nThese are NOT official public APIs. They were captured by observing network traffic while using the site.\n\n**Important:**\n- Auth tokens in `auth.json` may expire — re-capture if you get 401 errors\n- Internal APIs can change without notice — endpoints may break\n- Rate limits are unknown — be conservative with request frequency\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Access Trustmrr data without official API access\n- Automate actions on trustmrr.com (faster than browser automation)\n- Call the same endpoints the Trustmrr frontend uses\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```typescript\nimport { TrustmrrClient } from \"./scripts/api.ts\";\n\n// Load captured auth from auth.json\nconst client = await TrustmrrClient.fromAuthFile(\"auth.json\");\n\n// Make requests to internal endpoints\nconst result = await client.get(\"/endpoint\");\n```\n\n## Captured Authentication\n\nThe `auth.json` file contains credentials extracted from browser traffic:\n- **Auth headers:** 3 (sec-fetch-storage-access, x-goog-api-key, x-youtube-ad-signals)\n- **Session cookies:** 7\n\nIf auth expires, re-run `unbrowse_login` or `unbrowse_capture` to refresh tokens.\n\n## Internal Endpoints (370)\n\n\n## Error Handling\n\n```typescript\ntry {\n  const data = await client.get(\"/resource\");\n} catch (err) {\n  if (err.message.includes(\"401\")) {\n    // Auth expired — need to re-capture\n    console.error(\"Auth expired, re-run unbrowse_login\");\n  } else {\n    console.error(\"API error:\", err.message);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSee [REFERENCE.md](references/REFERENCE.md) for detailed endpoint documentation.\n"
